1
00:00:04,470 --> 00:00:06,470
So you're going to take me every day?

2
00:00:06,470 --> 00:00:08,800
If you don't mind the hassle, I'd like to.

3
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:11,670
Then next time you come, wait inside the house.

4
00:00:11,670 --> 00:00:13,030
Don't stand out in the sun.

5
00:00:13,670 --> 00:00:14,870
What are you doing, Din?

6
00:00:14,870 --> 00:00:17,330
I just wanted to try guessing.

7
00:00:17,330 --> 00:00:19,530
But when you said you didn't want to see me,

8
00:00:19,530 --> 00:00:20,870
I was lost.

9
00:00:20,870 --> 00:00:21,930
You should go, Physics.

10
00:00:21,930 --> 00:00:25,100
I can't imagine what I'd be without you.

11
00:00:25,100 --> 00:00:25,970
I like you, Physics.

12
00:00:25,970 --> 00:00:27,100
Come to England with me.

13
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:28,670
Well, every plan in my life...

14
00:00:28,670 --> 00:00:30,230
has always had you in it.

15
00:00:30,230 --> 00:00:32,170
I don't know how to tell my parents.

16
00:00:32,170 --> 00:00:34,000
Rei, you fucker. What about the baby?

17
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:35,600
Huh? That's your kid, asshole.

18
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:38,530
This is between me and Mii. Stay the fuck out of it.

19
00:00:38,530 --> 00:00:39,800
Then tell me, Mii,

20
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:41,230
what you want me to do.

21
00:00:41,230 --> 00:00:42,800
Fine. I'll tell you.

22
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:44,470
Get out of my life.

23
00:00:44,470 --> 00:00:47,800
Do you know your words and your actions don't match?

24
00:00:47,800 --> 00:00:50,430
You say you didn't mean to leave me,

25
00:00:50,430 --> 00:00:51,430
but you did.

26
00:00:51,430 --> 00:00:54,000
My friend was in trouble. I couldn't leave my friend.

27
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:55,200
Couldn't leave your friend.

28
00:00:55,800 --> 00:00:57,070
But you could leave me.

29
00:00:57,070 --> 00:00:58,730
I can't trust you anymore.

30
00:00:58,730 --> 00:00:59,700
I've had enough

31
00:00:59,700 --> 00:01:01,300
of everything about you.

32
00:01:01,300 --> 00:01:02,530
This is my last warning.

33
00:01:02,530 --> 00:01:03,600
Leave my brother alone.

34
00:01:04,129 --> 00:01:05,300
Physics, but...

35
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:07,000
Hey! Physics!

36
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:09,330
You can hit me as many times as you want.

37
00:01:09,930 --> 00:01:11,630
But can't you give me a chance?

38
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:20,800
Oh, hello. / Hello.

39
00:01:21,530 --> 00:01:24,030
Oh, bye-bye.

40
00:01:31,430 --> 00:01:32,470
Hey!

41
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:42,330
Let me help pick them up.

42
00:01:43,570 --> 00:01:44,930
It's okay.

43
00:01:58,600 --> 00:01:59,970
Din!

44
00:01:59,970 --> 00:02:02,770
Star, what's wrong this time?

45
00:02:06,170 --> 00:02:07,730
What happened in there?

46
00:02:08,030 --> 00:02:09,570
Din, let's just go.

47
00:02:09,570 --> 00:02:11,000
I'll tell you later.

48
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:07,270
Why didn't you tell me sooner, Star?

49
00:04:07,870 --> 00:04:09,700
It's really dangerous, you know?

50
00:04:13,400 --> 00:04:15,100
I'm sorry, Din.

51
00:04:15,570 --> 00:04:17,829
I thought he was just messing around.

52
00:04:18,570 --> 00:04:21,200
And nothing like this has happened in a long time.

53
00:04:21,200 --> 00:04:23,570
I think we should tell your dad about this.

54
00:04:23,570 --> 00:04:25,500
So he can help if anything happens.

55
00:04:25,500 --> 00:04:27,030
Please don't, Din.

56
00:04:27,600 --> 00:04:30,470
If you tell my dad, it'll turn into a big deal.

57
00:04:30,470 --> 00:04:32,030
But... / Please.

58
00:04:33,370 --> 00:04:34,870
I'll change my class time

59
00:04:34,870 --> 00:04:36,900
or switch rooms.

60
00:04:36,900 --> 00:04:39,330
So no one has to worry.

61
00:04:39,930 --> 00:04:41,470
Please, Din.

62
00:04:48,170 --> 00:04:51,400
Then from now on, I'll take you to class every day

63
00:04:51,400 --> 00:04:53,270
and wait to pick you up, too.

64
00:04:55,630 --> 00:04:57,230
Thank you.

65
00:04:58,370 --> 00:04:59,570
Hungry?

66
00:05:01,670 --> 00:05:03,200
A little.

67
00:05:03,770 --> 00:05:06,170
Then eat something to take your mind off it.

68
00:05:08,770 --> 00:05:10,900
Are you really okay, Din?

69
00:05:12,930 --> 00:05:14,870
I'm okay with the food.

70
00:05:14,870 --> 00:05:17,070
But I'm not okay with what happened.

71
00:05:25,870 --> 00:05:27,800
It's fine. Eat up.

72
00:05:39,830 --> 00:05:44,270
Star, I'll be right here with you.

73
00:05:48,300 --> 00:05:50,330
Thank you, Din.

74
00:06:14,630 --> 00:06:15,970
Ooh! / Hey!

75
00:06:15,970 --> 00:06:17,270
Why'd you hit me?

76
00:06:26,230 --> 00:06:28,270
Is this yours? / Hm.

77
00:06:30,430 --> 00:06:34,770
Brot you some snaks. Enjoy.

78
00:06:35,130 --> 00:06:36,800
Where do you think he's from?

79
00:06:36,800 --> 00:06:38,900
Not from Bangkok, I bet.

80
00:06:56,870 --> 00:06:58,900
You think it's him, right?

81
00:06:58,900 --> 00:07:02,000
You-know-who.

82
00:07:03,530 --> 00:07:06,070
Mm, that's him.

83
00:07:07,200 --> 00:07:10,800
Do you think we're like dogs or what?

84
00:07:14,700 --> 00:07:18,530
Let him do whatever he wants. Don't worry about me.

85
00:07:18,530 --> 00:07:20,700
I don't want to go back anymore.

86
00:07:24,730 --> 00:07:26,730
Here, eat up. / For real?

87
00:07:27,030 --> 00:07:29,570
It'll all be gone by evening. / Just take it.

88
00:07:29,830 --> 00:07:31,070
Thanks, bro.

89
00:07:47,300 --> 00:07:49,570
Oh, gather up! We're done!

90
00:07:51,500 --> 00:07:53,670
Sit, sit, sit.

91
00:07:57,130 --> 00:07:58,730
The real match is soon.

92
00:08:00,170 --> 00:08:03,030
So get plenty of rest these days.

93
00:08:03,530 --> 00:08:06,170
As for the M.6 students taking university exams,

94
00:08:06,170 --> 00:08:08,730
don't push yourselves too hard training.

95
00:08:09,730 --> 00:08:12,430
Go on, we're done! Go home and rest!

96
00:08:13,830 --> 00:08:15,770
See you, everyone. Thank you.

97
00:08:15,770 --> 00:08:16,870
See ya.

98
00:08:17,770 --> 00:08:19,770
Go home. / See you, man.

99
00:08:23,200 --> 00:08:24,870
Thanop, see ya. / Get home safe.

100
00:08:26,070 --> 00:08:27,830
See ya, man. / Bye, sir.

101
00:08:28,130 --> 00:08:30,300
Coach, can you stay a bit longer? / What?

102
00:08:30,300 --> 00:08:33,500
Can you stay and help me practice shooting?

103
00:08:33,500 --> 00:08:35,200
At this hour? / Yes.

104
00:08:35,330 --> 00:08:36,169
Oh, well.

105
00:08:36,169 --> 00:08:38,870
Jay, are you in a hurry to get home?

106
00:08:39,030 --> 00:08:39,630
Hm?

107
00:08:40,500 --> 00:08:41,630
Go play keeper for me.

108
00:08:42,730 --> 00:08:44,270
Me? / Yeah.

109
00:08:47,030 --> 00:08:48,130
Fine, just for a bit.

110
00:08:48,130 --> 00:08:49,770
Go on, just for a bit.

111
00:08:49,770 --> 00:08:50,930
Shooting practice.

112
00:08:50,930 --> 00:08:53,100
The most important thing in shooting

113
00:08:53,100 --> 00:08:54,370
is a solid stance.

114
00:08:54,970 --> 00:08:56,630
You're hot-headed.

115
00:08:56,630 --> 00:08:59,870
You need to stay calm and look at the goal.

116
00:08:59,870 --> 00:09:03,200
Think of the goal as your target,

117
00:09:03,200 --> 00:09:06,200
the future you have to step into.

118
00:09:06,200 --> 00:09:08,730
The moment you see an opening, shoot.

119
00:10:16,830 --> 00:10:18,170
Hello, Mii.

120
00:10:18,170 --> 00:10:20,270
Aof, I talked to my parents.

121
00:10:20,270 --> 00:10:24,470
Honestly, I feel so relieved. They scolded me a bit.

122
00:10:24,470 --> 00:10:27,370
But at least I don't have to deal with it alone.

123
00:10:27,370 --> 00:10:29,300
Mm, good.

124
00:10:29,300 --> 00:10:31,130
So are you going anywhere today?

125
00:10:31,130 --> 00:10:33,930
I'm going to the hospital with my dad.

126
00:10:33,930 --> 00:10:36,100
And once everything's done,

127
00:10:36,100 --> 00:10:37,600
I'm taking the little one

128
00:10:37,600 --> 00:10:40,070
to Australia to raise it with my aunt.

129
00:10:41,500 --> 00:10:43,100
Don't be reckless, Mii.

130
00:10:43,100 --> 00:10:44,800
Or the little one might get hurt.

131
00:10:44,800 --> 00:10:49,500
Don't worry, Aof. I'm fine. Thank you, dear Aof.

132
00:11:12,270 --> 00:11:13,100
Mom.

133
00:11:14,030 --> 00:11:16,870
Isn't this way too much?

134
00:11:16,870 --> 00:11:19,130
This could feed the whole neighborhood.

135
00:11:19,970 --> 00:11:21,300
It's not too much.

136
00:11:21,300 --> 00:11:24,370
I'll hand some out to the neighbors and it'll be gone.

137
00:11:24,830 --> 00:11:26,500
See, the whole neighborhood.

138
00:11:27,100 --> 00:11:30,300
Oh, take some over to Fuen's place, too.

139
00:11:31,200 --> 00:11:32,730
Sure, Mom.

140
00:11:35,970 --> 00:11:39,630
Did you accept the UK university's offer yet?

141
00:11:39,970 --> 00:11:43,000
The university... Oh, I've accepted.

142
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:45,830
I just got the confirmation email this morning.

143
00:11:47,130 --> 00:11:52,770
And Fuen agreed to go to England with you, right?

144
00:11:54,830 --> 00:11:56,330
Yes.

145
00:11:56,330 --> 00:11:59,830
Great. I'll look for a language course for him.

146
00:11:59,830 --> 00:12:02,500
Oh, sure. Sure.

147
00:12:03,500 --> 00:12:04,700
And what about you?

148
00:12:05,530 --> 00:12:08,170
Want to take a fun class over the break?

149
00:12:08,170 --> 00:12:09,730
How about languages?

150
00:12:11,130 --> 00:12:13,200
Maybe not languages yet, bro.

151
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:19,000
But... can I take singing lessons?

152
00:12:21,330 --> 00:12:24,970
Please, Mom, I really want to learn.

153
00:12:27,900 --> 00:12:29,670
Okay, okay. Fine.

154
00:12:30,400 --> 00:12:34,130
Go find what you want to learn, where, and with who. / Okay.

155
00:12:34,130 --> 00:12:35,630
Show it to me first.

156
00:12:35,630 --> 00:12:37,100
Or should I find one for you?

157
00:12:37,500 --> 00:12:39,330
No, I'm good.

158
00:12:39,670 --> 00:12:43,300
Last time, I had you learn country music.

159
00:12:43,300 --> 00:12:44,700
With Kru Sala, no less.

160
00:12:45,530 --> 00:12:48,370
Okay, okay, go find one and show me. Okay?

161
00:12:48,370 --> 00:12:49,870
Okay.

162
00:12:49,870 --> 00:12:51,670
Thank you, Mom.

163
00:12:55,430 --> 00:12:58,370
Just study hard. That's all I need.

164
00:12:58,370 --> 00:12:59,530
Yes, dear. / Okay.

165
00:12:59,530 --> 00:13:00,830
Okay, sweetie? / Sure.

166
00:13:00,830 --> 00:13:03,230
Let's get back to it. I'll take some to Fuen.

167
00:13:03,900 --> 00:13:04,930
Done yet?

168
00:13:04,930 --> 00:13:06,030
Been at it a while.

169
00:13:18,830 --> 00:13:21,100
You're really not taking the med exam?

170
00:13:22,970 --> 00:13:25,100
Let me be stubborn about this one, Mom.

171
00:13:30,030 --> 00:13:31,670
Engineering it is, then.

172
00:13:31,670 --> 00:13:34,300
If you think you can do it, it's your call.

173
00:13:35,670 --> 00:13:36,700
Thank you.

174
00:13:36,700 --> 00:13:38,170
Are you going anywhere later?

175
00:13:38,170 --> 00:13:40,030
I'm meeting a friend tonight, Mom.

176
00:13:40,030 --> 00:13:41,700
Oh my, are you seeing someone?

177
00:13:41,700 --> 00:13:43,770
Hey, not yet.

178
00:13:43,770 --> 00:13:47,700
Don't date yet. Focus on university for now, understand?

179
00:13:48,170 --> 00:13:49,770
I'm heading out in a bit.

180
00:13:49,770 --> 00:13:52,030
I'm meeting Auntie Pat, okay?

181
00:13:52,030 --> 00:13:53,100
Okay.

182
00:14:11,370 --> 00:14:13,200
You haven't left yet, Mom?

183
00:14:16,700 --> 00:14:18,130
Did you forget something?

184
00:14:25,530 --> 00:14:28,630
Din, I need your advice on something.

185
00:14:29,130 --> 00:14:30,900
Can I come in?

186
00:14:44,470 --> 00:14:46,700
Have you talked to Physics about this?

187
00:14:48,630 --> 00:14:49,700
Not yet.

188
00:14:50,700 --> 00:14:52,400
If he knows I'm stressed,

189
00:14:52,400 --> 00:14:54,130
he'll overthink it again.

190
00:14:55,600 --> 00:14:58,600
But you should tell him what you're thinking.

191
00:14:58,900 --> 00:15:01,370
But I don't know where to start.

192
00:15:02,630 --> 00:15:05,070
Physics has helped me so much.

193
00:15:05,070 --> 00:15:06,500
Taking me to classes,

194
00:15:06,500 --> 00:15:08,500
tutoring me on the side.

195
00:15:08,500 --> 00:15:10,870
His family supports me all the way, too.

196
00:15:11,800 --> 00:15:13,030
That's why I'm scared.

197
00:15:13,730 --> 00:15:15,630
Because if I don't get in,

198
00:15:15,630 --> 00:15:17,830
he'll start thinking crazy things again.

199
00:15:25,070 --> 00:15:28,370
That day, he showed me a bunch of universities.

200
00:15:28,830 --> 00:15:30,970
There was one I really liked,

201
00:15:31,570 --> 00:15:33,600
but it's not in London.

202
00:15:34,200 --> 00:15:36,000
And the one that is in London,

203
00:15:36,470 --> 00:15:39,630
I don't think I'll get in this year.

204
00:15:42,230 --> 00:15:43,670
So what do you think, Fuen?

205
00:15:44,330 --> 00:15:47,430
Study together, or somewhere else?

206
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:52,000
Honestly, they're both Architecture.

207
00:15:52,530 --> 00:15:54,170
Anywhere is fine.

208
00:15:55,370 --> 00:15:59,770
But if we're going together, the same city is easier.

209
00:16:03,730 --> 00:16:07,600
I haven't even told my parents I'm going.

210
00:16:07,600 --> 00:16:09,270
Then tell them first.

211
00:16:10,130 --> 00:16:12,600
And for art programs,

212
00:16:12,600 --> 00:16:15,130
you need a portfolio, right? Have you made one?

213
00:16:15,130 --> 00:16:18,170
Did you keep the stuff you used to draw for fun?

214
00:16:19,170 --> 00:16:21,930
I have some, but it's all over the place.

215
00:16:22,600 --> 00:16:24,200
I just draw whatever.

216
00:16:25,570 --> 00:16:28,670
But I kept the designs I helped my dad with.

217
00:16:28,670 --> 00:16:31,430
That's fine. They just need to be in the same group.

218
00:16:32,030 --> 00:16:35,730
And when you're free, go check out the seniors' work at uni.

219
00:16:35,730 --> 00:16:39,670
Like open houses or thesis shows.

220
00:16:40,070 --> 00:16:45,070
Man, coming to you was the right call. Thanks a lot.

221
00:16:45,930 --> 00:16:48,830
And you're applying with a portfolio too, right?

222
00:16:49,730 --> 00:16:50,730
Mm.

223
00:16:51,230 --> 00:16:53,030
But not for med school.

224
00:16:53,430 --> 00:16:54,430
Hey!

225
00:16:55,830 --> 00:16:57,300
I still want engineering.

226
00:16:57,300 --> 00:16:58,600
Mm.

227
00:16:58,600 --> 00:17:01,470
My mom's a little sulky about it, too.

228
00:17:01,470 --> 00:17:02,870
But she didn't say anything.

229
00:17:03,700 --> 00:17:05,329
What's there to say?

230
00:17:05,329 --> 00:17:08,430
You'll get in somewhere. I'm not worried about you.

231
00:17:08,430 --> 00:17:10,000
Worry about me.

232
00:17:10,970 --> 00:17:12,800
Let's hope so.

233
00:17:14,099 --> 00:17:17,730
Thanks a lot. I'm off, then. Thank you.

234
00:17:54,600 --> 00:17:56,500
Say whatever it is.

235
00:18:05,700 --> 00:18:08,100
Dad, Mom...

236
00:18:12,100 --> 00:18:15,230
Can I go study abroad with Physics?

237
00:18:24,200 --> 00:18:25,800
Son,

238
00:18:27,130 --> 00:18:29,970
your English is still a disaster.

239
00:18:32,630 --> 00:18:34,600
Let me ask you something.

240
00:18:34,600 --> 00:18:38,400
Do you want to go because you really want to study?

241
00:18:38,770 --> 00:18:40,900
Or because of Physics?

242
00:18:42,500 --> 00:18:46,170
At first it was because of him. Now it's both.

243
00:18:46,170 --> 00:18:48,670
I'm working really hard at my tutoring classes.

244
00:18:48,670 --> 00:18:51,570
And Physics's mom is helping me with a lot of things.

245
00:18:51,900 --> 00:18:57,500
Dad, Mom, I don't know if I'll get in.

246
00:18:57,500 --> 00:18:59,470
But I'm trying.

247
00:19:04,470 --> 00:19:05,730
Fuen, sweetie.

248
00:19:06,400 --> 00:19:12,370
If you don't get in, that's okay. We'll do a course.

249
00:19:12,370 --> 00:19:16,400
You don't mind if I don't graduate with everyone else?

250
00:19:16,400 --> 00:19:21,430
Son, your dad and I are ready to support you.

251
00:19:21,430 --> 00:19:24,530
We'll pay for your studies, for your dream,

252
00:19:24,530 --> 00:19:26,670
for your happiness, my son.

253
00:19:27,300 --> 00:19:32,500
Fuen, listen to me. I'm being serious.

254
00:19:36,500 --> 00:19:38,630
Since you're running off together,

255
00:19:40,130 --> 00:19:43,030
tell his parents to come ask properly.

256
00:19:43,030 --> 00:19:44,070
Dad!

257
00:19:45,430 --> 00:19:47,030
Brilliant, honey.

258
00:19:47,330 --> 00:19:48,730
Oh, you too, Mom?

259
00:19:48,730 --> 00:19:50,600
Most brilliant idea ever, honey.

260
00:19:53,630 --> 00:19:55,670
I was worried sick before asking.

261
00:19:58,400 --> 00:19:59,900
That's all it took, son.

262
00:20:16,870 --> 00:20:19,170
Meet me here after class.

263
00:20:19,170 --> 00:20:21,800
Oh, won't you get bored?

264
00:20:21,800 --> 00:20:24,100
My class is two whole hours.

265
00:20:27,130 --> 00:20:30,170
Don't worry. I've got stuff to do while I wait.

266
00:20:30,170 --> 00:20:31,300
Go on to class.

267
00:20:31,300 --> 00:20:32,770
Okay.

268
00:20:35,830 --> 00:20:36,830
Star!

269
00:20:37,530 --> 00:20:38,530
Yeah?

270
00:20:40,030 --> 00:20:42,630
Focus on class. Don't worry.

271
00:21:17,170 --> 00:21:19,700
You can stop trying to guess.

272
00:21:19,700 --> 00:21:21,470
Even if you get some letters right,

273
00:21:21,470 --> 00:21:25,100
you'll never guess the last three.

274
00:21:26,100 --> 00:21:27,670
Is it that obvious on my face?

275
00:21:34,870 --> 00:21:39,670
I'm off to class, then, Guardian Din.

276
00:21:51,300 --> 00:21:53,370
Is my face really that obvious?

277
00:22:06,300 --> 00:22:07,700
What are you reading?

278
00:22:09,630 --> 00:22:15,600
Oh, I'm looking at the university you want to get into.

279
00:22:15,600 --> 00:22:17,770
What exams you need.

280
00:22:22,800 --> 00:22:26,100
As far as I remember, for your IELTS,

281
00:22:26,100 --> 00:22:30,730
you need around 5.5 to 6.5, depending on the program.

282
00:22:32,230 --> 00:22:33,670
Whoa.

283
00:22:33,670 --> 00:22:37,500
And these are the A-Levels you need for admission.

284
00:22:40,500 --> 00:22:42,870
No room for me falling short, huh?

285
00:22:46,000 --> 00:22:49,470
I don't want to pressure you.

286
00:22:51,570 --> 00:22:54,100
Or if you don't get in this year,

287
00:22:54,100 --> 00:22:57,230
why not take a language course for a year?

288
00:22:57,870 --> 00:23:01,600
Hey, don't lower your expectations yet.

289
00:23:02,300 --> 00:23:08,770
Aim for the university first. If it fails, we'll see.

290
00:23:16,670 --> 00:23:18,470
Tired?

291
00:23:21,870 --> 00:23:25,330
Tired... but I'm not giving up.

292
00:23:39,200 --> 00:23:41,530
Thanks for trying so hard for me.

293
00:24:13,670 --> 00:24:14,830
Din!

294
00:24:18,170 --> 00:24:20,570
I told you I'd wait right here.

295
00:24:24,800 --> 00:24:26,630
Come on, let's go home.

296
00:24:37,370 --> 00:24:40,530
Din, um...

297
00:24:41,270 --> 00:24:43,800
Can I ask you something personal?

298
00:24:43,800 --> 00:24:47,130
Mm, sure. What do you want to know?

299
00:24:48,700 --> 00:24:53,470
You and Yok... are you two still...

300
00:25:05,670 --> 00:25:07,500
We're not anything anymore.

301
00:25:08,470 --> 00:25:11,730
At most, we're just acquaintances.

302
00:25:14,700 --> 00:25:17,870
If you want to know anything else, just ask me.

303
00:25:17,870 --> 00:25:19,830
I'll answer everything.

304
00:25:22,000 --> 00:25:23,100
Okay.

305
00:25:24,130 --> 00:25:25,670
That's all.

306
00:25:27,170 --> 00:25:30,400
But are you in a hurry this evening?

307
00:25:31,730 --> 00:25:34,430
My dad's inviting you to dinner.

308
00:25:36,670 --> 00:25:39,000
And he specifically said

309
00:25:39,000 --> 00:25:40,900
you have to come.

310
00:25:40,900 --> 00:25:42,100
Your dad...

311
00:25:42,730 --> 00:25:44,630
Your dad's inviting me to dinner?

312
00:25:45,370 --> 00:25:46,930
Yes.

313
00:25:48,200 --> 00:25:50,500
Shall we hurry, then?

314
00:25:50,500 --> 00:25:53,530
My dad's really strict, Din.

315
00:25:53,530 --> 00:25:55,530
Let's go, let's go eat!

316
00:26:09,900 --> 00:26:13,070
Come, eat. I made plenty.

317
00:26:13,500 --> 00:26:15,930
Here, take the shrimp first.

318
00:26:15,930 --> 00:26:17,770
You're good at peeling, huh?

319
00:26:19,470 --> 00:26:20,300
Yeah.

320
00:26:20,800 --> 00:26:22,430
So, Din,

321
00:26:22,670 --> 00:26:25,970
your exams are coming up. Studying hard?

322
00:26:25,970 --> 00:26:27,270
Pretty much.

323
00:26:27,270 --> 00:26:29,070
But I'll try the portfolio round first.

324
00:26:29,070 --> 00:26:30,800
If I get in, I'll just take it.

325
00:26:30,800 --> 00:26:32,730
Mm, good idea.

326
00:26:32,730 --> 00:26:35,330
Is it a university you already like?

327
00:26:35,330 --> 00:26:37,800
Yes. I looked at the curriculum and loved it.

328
00:26:37,800 --> 00:26:40,570
I think studying there would be fun.

329
00:26:40,570 --> 00:26:44,900
Mm, good. Study somewhere you like.

330
00:26:45,430 --> 00:26:48,070
And do you think first year will be tough?

331
00:26:49,730 --> 00:26:51,770
I'm not sure.

332
00:26:52,530 --> 00:26:53,600
Star!

333
00:26:54,030 --> 00:26:55,700
He'll be studying hard,

334
00:26:56,230 --> 00:26:58,330
so no whining, got it?

335
00:26:59,000 --> 00:27:00,530
Dad!

336
00:27:02,400 --> 00:27:05,470
Din, peel some shrimp for me too, son.

337
00:27:11,470 --> 00:27:14,030
Here you go, sir. All peeled.

338
00:27:15,030 --> 00:27:17,470
As skilled as they say.

339
00:27:53,670 --> 00:27:55,200
Homework. I'll hand it in.

340
00:27:55,200 --> 00:27:56,730
Oh, yeah.

341
00:28:01,130 --> 00:28:02,300
Thank you.

342
00:28:47,130 --> 00:28:48,230
What?

343
00:28:48,570 --> 00:28:51,400
I'm glad to see you working hard at something.

344
00:28:51,800 --> 00:28:54,530
But take a break. Too much isn't good.

345
00:28:55,000 --> 00:28:57,570
But you know, if I can't pull it off this time...

346
00:29:00,070 --> 00:29:01,400
Don't think like that.

347
00:29:01,400 --> 00:29:02,800
You can do it.

348
00:29:03,370 --> 00:29:05,470
Just stay as cocky as usual.

349
00:29:06,200 --> 00:29:08,500
Tang, are you insulting me?

350
00:29:09,630 --> 00:29:10,630
Isn't it wet?

351
00:29:11,870 --> 00:29:14,170
Oh, I'll probably be late on match day.

352
00:29:14,170 --> 00:29:15,730
I'm going to an open house first.

353
00:29:15,730 --> 00:29:16,970
Up to you.

354
00:29:17,530 --> 00:29:19,200
Honestly, you don't have to come.

355
00:29:19,430 --> 00:29:21,570
You're not that important to me anyway.

356
00:29:22,800 --> 00:29:26,870
But you're a footballer. Why are you swimming?

357
00:29:27,700 --> 00:29:29,970
You never really get me, do you?

358
00:29:30,300 --> 00:29:33,070
I swim so my lungs get stronger.

359
00:29:33,500 --> 00:29:35,830
So I can run all day, morning to night.

360
00:29:36,630 --> 00:29:37,970
Get it?

361
00:29:39,370 --> 00:29:41,070
Talking to you is a waste of time.

362
00:29:41,070 --> 00:29:42,930
I'm going back to swimming.

363
00:29:52,070 --> 00:29:54,170
Who the hell could understand you?

364
00:29:54,800 --> 00:29:57,770
Your brain's gone to mush.

365
00:30:07,330 --> 00:30:11,170
Number 14, Aof, has really grown up, Coach.

366
00:30:11,900 --> 00:30:13,130
You think so, sir?

367
00:30:13,130 --> 00:30:14,130
Yeah.

368
00:30:27,070 --> 00:30:29,030
Come on! Woo!

369
00:30:29,030 --> 00:30:31,070
I think so too.

370
00:30:51,000 --> 00:30:52,500
Probably needs to poop.

371
00:30:52,500 --> 00:30:54,930
Players always need to poop after scoring.

372
00:30:54,930 --> 00:30:56,000
Happens to me a lot.

373
00:30:56,330 --> 00:30:58,970
So Ronaldo would be pooping all match?

374
00:30:58,970 --> 00:31:01,000
Keep practicing, come on!

375
00:31:02,100 --> 00:31:03,170
Physics!

376
00:31:04,100 --> 00:31:05,700
You came to watch me?

377
00:31:08,570 --> 00:31:11,470
Just stopped by to watch you play.

378
00:31:13,000 --> 00:31:17,430
So what's your next plan?

379
00:31:18,200 --> 00:31:21,530
You sneak my brother home every day.

380
00:31:21,530 --> 00:31:23,230
You think I don't know?

381
00:31:25,430 --> 00:31:27,300
You knew?

382
00:31:27,630 --> 00:31:28,730
Mm.

383
00:31:29,630 --> 00:31:31,270
My mom knows, too.

384
00:31:33,800 --> 00:31:36,470
How long are you going to avoid looking at me?

385
00:31:36,470 --> 00:31:39,170
I'm not your dad. I'm your friend.

386
00:31:45,900 --> 00:31:47,100
Not talking? I'm leaving.

387
00:31:47,100 --> 00:31:47,900
Physics!

388
00:31:48,870 --> 00:31:50,000
Um...

389
00:31:53,400 --> 00:31:55,970
Just you not stopping me makes me really happy.

390
00:32:11,400 --> 00:32:13,870
The reason I never gave you a chance

391
00:32:14,830 --> 00:32:16,070
is you being an ass.

392
00:32:17,470 --> 00:32:18,900
And you're all talk,

393
00:32:18,900 --> 00:32:20,570
you never really show it.

394
00:32:20,900 --> 00:32:25,570
But this time, you're proving it to everyone around you.

395
00:32:25,570 --> 00:32:26,730
Not just me.

396
00:32:29,670 --> 00:32:30,730
Well?

397
00:32:30,730 --> 00:32:32,030
You gonna stay quiet?

398
00:32:34,500 --> 00:32:36,430
Well? Are you going to ask?

399
00:32:39,070 --> 00:32:41,330
Then let me court your brother again, Physics.

400
00:32:41,330 --> 00:32:42,530
Physics, I'm begging you.

401
00:32:42,530 --> 00:32:44,270
Okay, okay, you can. / Really?

402
00:32:45,230 --> 00:32:46,100
Yes, you can!

403
00:32:46,470 --> 00:32:49,300
But I won't if you keep messing around like this.

404
00:32:49,300 --> 00:32:50,570
Okay, okay, okay.

405
00:32:51,100 --> 00:32:52,600
I give up, I give up.

406
00:32:58,470 --> 00:32:59,800
Fine, I'll allow it.

407
00:33:00,900 --> 00:33:02,870
But don't hurt my brother again.

408
00:33:02,870 --> 00:33:03,870
Got it.

409
00:33:04,100 --> 00:33:06,630
Make him cry again and you'll get it again.

410
00:33:09,000 --> 00:33:12,530
But whether Chemi lets you court him, you'll have to ask him.

411
00:33:13,600 --> 00:33:15,900
That's all I can do as his brother.

412
00:33:16,470 --> 00:33:18,830
Mm, I love you, Physics. Thanks so much.

413
00:33:18,830 --> 00:33:20,130
Hey, go practice.

414
00:33:20,130 --> 00:33:20,770
True friend.

415
00:33:20,770 --> 00:33:24,470
Give me a kiss. Physics, Physics, give me a kiss.

416
00:33:34,500 --> 00:33:37,830
One, two, three... Yay!

417
00:33:38,700 --> 00:33:39,700
Chemi!

418
00:33:46,230 --> 00:33:48,230
Can I talk to you for a moment?

419
00:33:50,370 --> 00:33:52,030
Just a minute.

420
00:33:57,030 --> 00:33:59,000
If there's something, just say it.

421
00:34:01,530 --> 00:34:03,430
I've got a big match this Sunday.

422
00:34:04,170 --> 00:34:05,630
Will you come watch me?

423
00:34:08,900 --> 00:34:10,130
I'm busy.

424
00:34:16,070 --> 00:34:18,130
Is that all you wanted to say?

425
00:34:18,400 --> 00:34:19,800
I understand

426
00:34:21,000 --> 00:34:23,630
that you won't forgive me.

427
00:34:24,030 --> 00:34:26,530
But can I have one more chance?

428
00:34:26,530 --> 00:34:28,500
Even if it's the last one.

429
00:34:29,800 --> 00:34:32,570
I want you to see that I've really changed.

430
00:34:40,670 --> 00:34:41,900
I told you,

431
00:34:42,400 --> 00:34:44,570
I don't want anything from you anymore.

432
00:34:45,130 --> 00:34:46,600
Stop forcing yourself.

433
00:34:46,600 --> 00:34:48,400
I'm not forcing anything.

434
00:34:50,500 --> 00:34:52,330
Today I realized...

435
00:34:53,000 --> 00:34:55,630
not thinking things through ruined everything.

436
00:34:56,600 --> 00:35:00,870
I kept making excuses so you'd forgive me like always.

437
00:35:01,300 --> 00:35:02,700
But now I get it.

438
00:35:02,700 --> 00:35:04,730
What I should do is apologize to you,

439
00:35:05,300 --> 00:35:07,400
and finally do what I say.

440
00:35:11,200 --> 00:35:13,170
Will you give me one more chance?

441
00:35:13,470 --> 00:35:14,930
Even if it's the last one.

442
00:35:16,030 --> 00:35:18,400
I promise, if I ruin it again this time,

443
00:35:18,830 --> 00:35:20,830
you'll never see my face again.

444
00:35:21,670 --> 00:35:26,330
♪ There's something in my heart I can't explain ♪

445
00:35:26,330 --> 00:35:30,670
♪ Still searching for someone to tell me ♪

446
00:35:30,670 --> 00:35:34,100
♪ No matter how much time goes by ♪

447
00:35:34,100 --> 00:35:36,300
♪ I never find what I'm looking for ♪

448
00:35:36,300 --> 00:35:41,000
♪ Why does my heart still feel so empty? ♪

449
00:35:46,830 --> 00:35:47,830
Mm.

450
00:35:49,100 --> 00:35:50,800
So what are you going to do?

451
00:35:51,200 --> 00:35:52,930
At the match this Sunday,

452
00:35:52,930 --> 00:35:54,930
I'll score five goals on my own.

453
00:35:54,930 --> 00:35:56,430
If I do...

454
00:35:56,800 --> 00:35:58,900
will you say yes?

455
00:35:58,900 --> 00:36:00,330
But if I don't,

456
00:36:00,330 --> 00:36:03,270
I promise you'll never see my face again.

457
00:36:16,100 --> 00:36:20,700
Up to you. But if you can't do it...

458
00:36:20,700 --> 00:36:22,900
please keep your promise

459
00:36:23,800 --> 00:36:25,900
that I'll never see you again.

460
00:36:34,400 --> 00:36:37,630
Okay, Chemi. I promise!

461
00:36:39,800 --> 00:36:45,400
♪ Every question in my heart has an answer now ♪

462
00:36:45,400 --> 00:36:52,270
♪ No matter how the story goes, in the end my answer is you ♪

463
00:37:12,730 --> 00:37:18,470
"You going with me tomorrow?"

464
00:37:23,930 --> 00:37:27,200
"I want to go a bit later."

465
00:37:27,200 --> 00:37:30,100
"I'll catch up."

466
00:37:30,100 --> 00:37:34,370
"Okay. Call me when you get there. I'll come get you."

467
00:37:42,570 --> 00:37:44,070
Thank you.

468
00:37:51,900 --> 00:37:53,170
We have to register today?

469
00:37:53,170 --> 00:37:55,230
Yeah. You haven't yet? / Not yet.

470
00:37:55,230 --> 00:37:56,830
The whole class has registered.

471
00:37:56,830 --> 00:37:58,470
If you don't register today,

472
00:37:58,470 --> 00:38:00,170
might have to wait till next year.

473
00:38:00,170 --> 00:38:01,470
Next year?

474
00:38:55,130 --> 00:38:57,530
"Dude, you coming to watch my match?"

475
00:39:03,070 --> 00:39:05,300
"I'll see."

476
00:39:06,700 --> 00:39:10,800
♪ When you said I was too young ♪

477
00:39:10,800 --> 00:39:18,900
♪ But it's okay, I'll still wait until that day ♪

478
00:39:18,900 --> 00:39:24,670
♪ The day you're here with me ♪

479
00:39:25,630 --> 00:39:30,800
♪ No matter how long it takes, my heart still calls for you ♪

480
00:39:30,800 --> 00:39:37,430
♪ Because this heart of mine is still waiting, only for you ♪

481
00:40:53,830 --> 00:40:55,330
What's on your mind?

482
00:40:56,300 --> 00:40:59,700
Thanop... today I want five goals on my own.

483
00:40:59,700 --> 00:41:03,300
Why five? Just winning the game is enough.

484
00:41:04,500 --> 00:41:06,430
I have to score five goals today

485
00:41:06,430 --> 00:41:08,700
to get another chance with Chemi.

486
00:41:10,100 --> 00:41:12,470
And you're betting it all on a match?

487
00:41:12,500 --> 00:41:13,870
Can you even handle it?

488
00:41:13,870 --> 00:41:15,900
I don't have any other choice.

489
00:41:16,830 --> 00:41:19,330
Football's the only thing I'm good at.

490
00:41:19,570 --> 00:41:21,330
If it were one of our past matches,

491
00:41:21,330 --> 00:41:23,230
I'd say we had a shot.

492
00:41:23,230 --> 00:41:27,130
But today we're up against Rei. Suan Mali.

493
00:41:28,330 --> 00:41:30,400
I have to pull it off, no matter what.

494
00:41:34,130 --> 00:41:36,170
Help me out, Thanop.

495
00:41:36,970 --> 00:41:39,100
You can't just ask me.

496
00:41:39,430 --> 00:41:41,170
Go tell the whole team.

497
00:41:53,530 --> 00:41:55,530
You sure know how to cause me trouble.

498
00:41:55,530 --> 00:41:58,370
So I have to plan for you to score alone, Aof?

499
00:41:58,400 --> 00:41:59,600
Huh?

500
00:41:59,600 --> 00:42:02,600
Well... yes, Coach.

501
00:42:03,100 --> 00:42:05,600
Aof, I can't let you do that.

502
00:42:05,600 --> 00:42:07,830
Or you'll be their target all game.

503
00:42:08,730 --> 00:42:09,870
Coach...

504
00:42:09,900 --> 00:42:11,470
What gives, Thanop?

505
00:42:11,470 --> 00:42:13,200
I send you to talk to him once,

506
00:42:13,200 --> 00:42:15,370
and you lose your head along with him?

507
00:42:15,400 --> 00:42:17,770
I really can't do that.

508
00:42:17,770 --> 00:42:19,700
Because if the team loses,

509
00:42:19,700 --> 00:42:22,470
all our training goes to waste. You know that?

510
00:42:22,470 --> 00:42:25,600
Yes. But no matter what, I have to win today.

511
00:42:26,070 --> 00:42:28,200
And I'll score five goals on my own.

512
00:42:28,200 --> 00:42:31,200
Coach, he's rarely this fired up.

513
00:42:31,200 --> 00:42:33,170
Coach, why not give him a shot?

514
00:42:46,670 --> 00:42:49,330
I can't decide this alone.

515
00:42:49,830 --> 00:42:50,970
What do you guys think?

516
00:42:51,300 --> 00:42:52,930
I agree.

517
00:42:54,130 --> 00:42:55,930
Me too.

518
00:42:56,770 --> 00:42:59,130
I told you I don't like watching football.

519
00:42:59,770 --> 00:43:01,770
And you still invited me.

520
00:43:04,100 --> 00:43:10,830
Hey, focus on this first. Deal with that later, okay?

521
00:43:16,170 --> 00:43:18,330
I know right now

522
00:43:18,730 --> 00:43:22,370
all you can think about is getting Aof five goals.

523
00:43:23,000 --> 00:43:26,230
But don't forget, safety matters too.

524
00:43:26,730 --> 00:43:29,200
I don't have much more to say.

525
00:43:29,830 --> 00:43:32,700
I'll be right here watching you succeed.

526
00:43:32,930 --> 00:43:33,930
Huddle up!

527
00:43:39,400 --> 00:43:42,300
Three, two, one... Thapfah!

528
00:45:29,200 --> 00:45:31,930
Don't rush in. Easy.

529
00:45:51,470 --> 00:45:53,370
Wait here. I'll be right back.

530
00:45:53,370 --> 00:45:55,000
Where to? / Need the toilet.

531
00:45:57,530 --> 00:45:59,130
You're leaving me here alone?

532
00:45:59,130 --> 00:46:00,370
Yeah, just for a bit.

533
00:46:22,430 --> 00:46:24,000
Fuen!

534
00:46:24,000 --> 00:46:25,870
What are you doing here?

535
00:46:25,870 --> 00:46:28,700
Same as you, checking out the work.

536
00:46:29,200 --> 00:46:31,170
No, I mean why are you here?

537
00:46:31,170 --> 00:46:32,570
Does Physics know?

538
00:46:33,200 --> 00:46:34,770
He'll get the wrong idea.

539
00:46:35,300 --> 00:46:36,530
He doesn't.

540
00:46:38,400 --> 00:46:40,130
Call him right now.

541
00:46:41,370 --> 00:46:43,100
My phone's dead.

542
00:46:43,100 --> 00:46:44,270
Use mine?

543
00:46:44,270 --> 00:46:45,830
Yeah, can I?

544
00:46:46,400 --> 00:46:49,370
Fuen! Tang! You guys came too?

545
00:46:49,370 --> 00:46:51,170
Come on, let's take a selfie.

546
00:46:53,970 --> 00:46:55,870
Didn't expect to see you here.

547
00:47:18,600 --> 00:47:20,830
Break, break, break. Get some water.

548
00:47:24,500 --> 00:47:26,300
Aof, just three more goals.

549
00:47:26,600 --> 00:47:27,800
You can't do it?

550
00:47:27,800 --> 00:47:28,800
Come on, fight.

551
00:47:28,800 --> 00:47:29,800
Yeah.

552
00:47:31,170 --> 00:47:33,970
I'm not surprised you're all this tired.

553
00:47:34,430 --> 00:47:37,730
I told you, what you're doing isn't easy at all.

554
00:47:37,730 --> 00:47:39,970
But I believe you can do it.

555
00:47:41,800 --> 00:47:44,100
We'll make a new plan for the second half.

556
00:47:44,930 --> 00:47:45,900
Fight or not?

557
00:47:45,900 --> 00:47:46,830
We'll fight!

558
00:47:48,400 --> 00:47:51,100
Here's the thing. Your problem right now

559
00:47:51,100 --> 00:47:53,000
is you're all rushing in too much.

560
00:47:53,000 --> 00:47:55,170
Time your runs better.

561
00:47:55,970 --> 00:47:57,400
Keep your heads.

562
00:47:57,400 --> 00:47:58,930
All out in the second half.

563
00:47:58,930 --> 00:47:59,930
Fight on!

564
00:47:59,930 --> 00:48:01,430
We'll fight! / Good.

565
00:48:02,030 --> 00:48:03,300
Take five.

566
00:48:18,000 --> 00:48:19,300
What are you guys doing?

567
00:48:20,930 --> 00:48:23,730
Nothing. Asking a friend about homework. Thanks a lot.

568
00:48:23,730 --> 00:48:24,500
Okay.

569
00:48:32,530 --> 00:48:33,700
Why so stressed?

570
00:50:32,800 --> 00:50:34,130
That's enough, Aof.

571
00:50:34,130 --> 00:50:35,670
I already gave you the chance.

572
00:50:36,200 --> 00:50:37,830
It's fine, Chemi.

573
00:50:37,830 --> 00:50:39,700
Keep watching me, Chemi.

574
00:50:43,600 --> 00:50:45,470
I'm going to make it happen.

575
00:50:45,470 --> 00:50:46,670
No, Aof.

576
00:50:50,100 --> 00:50:51,700
Look at your leg.

577
00:50:51,700 --> 00:50:54,070
What if you push it and it gets worse?

578
00:50:54,470 --> 00:50:55,430
I can still do it.

579
00:51:01,270 --> 00:51:05,630
Coach, let me take this penalty.

580
00:51:05,630 --> 00:51:11,030
I can still play. Trust me, Coach. Please.

581
00:51:11,630 --> 00:51:13,630
You're damn stubborn when you want to be.

582
00:51:13,630 --> 00:51:16,730
He can actually still play. I'll spray it for him.

583
00:51:16,730 --> 00:51:19,470
But if it hurts to put weight on it, stop right away.

584
00:51:26,670 --> 00:51:27,600
Careful.

585
00:53:14,830 --> 00:53:15,930
Sorry I'm late.

586
00:53:16,270 --> 00:53:17,400
The traffic was insane.

587
00:53:20,270 --> 00:53:21,930
Why didn't you pick up?

588
00:53:23,000 --> 00:53:25,830
Sorry. My phone died.

589
00:53:29,670 --> 00:53:31,730
How long are you going to keep lying?

590
00:53:34,570 --> 00:53:36,100
It really died.

591
00:53:42,430 --> 00:53:45,370
I really hate that we're like this right now.

592
00:53:50,700 --> 00:53:52,300
I'm sorry

593
00:53:54,170 --> 00:53:56,500
for forcing you to do something you don't like.

594
00:53:59,370 --> 00:54:01,000
If this is about today's event,

595
00:54:01,000 --> 00:54:03,470
I just went to look. I didn't do anything.

596
00:54:03,470 --> 00:54:05,370
Then why didn't you just tell me?

597
00:54:06,830 --> 00:54:08,170
Why hide it?

598
00:54:08,970 --> 00:54:11,370
I didn't think it was a big deal.

599
00:54:11,370 --> 00:54:14,370
And I didn't want you to get the wrong idea.

600
00:54:16,400 --> 00:54:18,170
You know what, Fuen?

601
00:54:18,700 --> 00:54:20,900
That reason makes no sense at all.

602
00:54:23,230 --> 00:54:26,270
I was so damn happy when you said you wanted to go together.

603
00:54:30,000 --> 00:54:31,830
What you're doing now...

604
00:54:34,800 --> 00:54:37,530
Is it just because you don't know how to say no to me?

605
00:55:02,430 --> 00:55:04,200
Think it over again.

606
00:55:07,600 --> 00:55:10,470
If you'd rather stay here, just tell me.

607
00:55:16,270 --> 00:55:17,830
You don't have to come with me.

608
00:55:25,130 --> 00:55:26,600
It's your life, Fuen.

609
00:55:28,100 --> 00:55:33,730
♪ Something has begun, and it's getting complicated ♪

610
00:55:33,730 --> 00:55:39,000
♪ There's more to it than that ♪

611
00:55:39,000 --> 00:55:47,730
♪ I can't find the answer ♪

612
00:55:49,800 --> 00:55:55,400
♪ If I'd known this was all the road we had ♪

613
00:55:55,400 --> 00:56:00,300
♪ I'd have spent that time making it count ♪

614
00:56:00,300 --> 00:56:06,530
♪ But in the end the story stops right here ♪

615
00:56:06,530 --> 00:56:11,670
♪ We'll never get to love each other again ♪

616
00:56:15,730 --> 00:56:21,570
♪ You and I were never meant to be ♪

617
00:56:25,270 --> 00:56:27,830
"Can you promise you won't let... Chemi get hurt? (Physics)"

618
00:56:27,830 --> 00:56:29,700
"I promise. (Aof)"

619
00:56:29,700 --> 00:56:31,270
"I'll wait till you're ready. (Aof)"

620
00:56:31,270 --> 00:56:33,070
"After the match. But win it for us"

621
00:56:33,070 --> 00:56:34,730
"and score at least five. (Chemi)"

622
00:56:34,730 --> 00:56:37,170
"What, Phoodin, in love? No, son, you're in M.6."

623
00:56:37,170 --> 00:56:39,530
"No love yet. Wait till university. (Din's Mom)"

624
00:56:39,970 --> 00:56:42,670
I don't know what will happen to us from here.

625
00:56:42,670 --> 00:56:45,670
This is the last time. I don't want to get hurt again.

626
00:56:46,700 --> 00:56:48,730
Aof, take good care of him.

627
00:56:48,730 --> 00:56:49,830
Yes, Mom.

628
00:56:54,770 --> 00:56:55,670
Hi, Mom.

629
00:56:55,670 --> 00:56:57,270
Is Physics home yet?

630
00:56:57,270 --> 00:56:58,270
He's not home yet.

631
00:56:58,270 --> 00:56:59,670
Didn't you two meet up?

632
00:57:01,030 --> 00:57:02,470
How is it? Tasty?

633
00:57:02,470 --> 00:57:03,530
It's good.

634
00:57:03,530 --> 00:57:05,870
I can feed myself. I'm almost done.

635
00:57:05,870 --> 00:57:08,370
Your hands hold the book, your eyes read it.

636
00:57:08,370 --> 00:57:10,200
As for your mouth, I'll feed you.

637
00:57:10,700 --> 00:57:11,800
Star!

638
00:57:11,930 --> 00:57:14,100
Hey! / What?

639
00:57:15,500 --> 00:57:16,730
Why are you running away?
